@startuml marked-fit
' How a search result's label and address are fitted so the match stays
' visible (ledger L5 R9).
skinparam defaultFontName "Noto Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #DDEBF7
  BorderColor #52687A
  ArrowColor #52687A
  FontColor #182734
}
title Fitting a search result so that its match shows

start
:mark = match_span(query, label), by the rules of search_score:
the first case-insensitive occurrence, else the first
word within the typo bound; <<#DDEBF7>>
:kept = the usual cut of the label (end cut);
if (kept shows all of mark?) then (yes)
  :label = kept, mark located in it; <<#E2EFDA>>
else (no)
  :label = a window around the mark,
  …context <b>mark</b> context…, the context split evenly,
  the left side taking the odd character; <<#FFF2CC>>
endif
if (the label shows a mark?) then (yes)
  :address = its usual cut (origin + path tail); <<#E2EFDA>>
  :mark the address's own match only where that cut shows it; <<#E2EFDA>>
else (no)
  :address = the URL cut if it shows the match,
  else a window around the address's match; <<#FFF2CC>>
endif
:HTML: escape(before), then the match in a mark element, then escape(after).
The match is coloured and underlined in accent,
which changes no width, so the fit stays exact; <<#FCE4D6>>
stop
@enduml
